  "question": {
    "text": "The magnetic flux through a loop of resistance $10 \\Omega$ is given by $\\phi=5 t^2-4 t+1$ Weber. How much current is induced in the loop after $0.2 \\mathrm{sec}$ ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ey1Fe",
      "text": "$0.4 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XHuso",
      "text": "$0.2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "g78gt",
      "text": "$0.04 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8bFKi",
      "text": "$0.02 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $\\phi=5 t^2-4 t+1$\n$$\n\\frac{d \\phi}{d t}=10 t-4\n$$\n$$\n\\mathrm{I}=\\frac{e}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{-d \\phi / d t}{\\mathrm{R}}=-\\frac{10 t-4}{10}\n$$\nAt $t=0.2 \\mathrm{sec}$\n$$\n\\mathrm{I}=\\frac{-(10 \\times 0.2-4)}{10}=-\\frac{(2-4)}{10}=+\\frac{2}{10}=+0.2 \\mathrm{~A}=0.2 \\mathrm{~A}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
